WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.330
Okay, this one has more of a story.

2
00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:06.900
One day Pastor, who went to primary and high school

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.650
with me, texts me and introduces me to César and Ale:

4
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:16.220
they were applying to a hackathon, needed one more,

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.640
and asked if I'd join them.

6
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.190
The old Juan would have said no

7
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:25.303
— out of shyness or laziness, I wouldn't have gone

8
00:00:25.303 --> 00:00:29.662
— but this time I thought the worst that could happen

9
00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:34.186
is they don't take us, and at the very least we'd learn

10
00:00:34.186 --> 00:00:34.680
a lot.

11
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.790
We came up with several ideas,

12
00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:39.181
and the one that won was Tripealo,

13
00:00:39.181 --> 00:00:42.697
a marketplace for travel experiences in Venezuela,

14
00:00:42.697 --> 00:00:45.580
and out of a thousand people who applied,

15
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:49.237
we were among the 100 who went to Yummy's offices in

16
00:00:49.237 --> 00:00:49.800
Caracas.

17
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.124
We didn't win, but I heard a lot of founders who now

18
00:00:54.124 --> 00:00:58.698
compete in Silicon Valley against the top US companies,

19
00:00:58.698 --> 00:01:02.440
and we came out with the drive to keep going.

20
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:07.830
They went on with Tripealo, and I went on with Abrahan,

21
00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.280
my co-founder at Salvalo.

22
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.063
Today Tripealo and Salvalo are both running,

23
00:01:14.063 --> 00:01:17.760
and I'm all in on Salvalo, in founder mode.

24
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.359
They're my founder bros now: together,

25
00:01:20.359 --> 00:01:23.300
but each on our own — Tripealo and Salvalo.

26
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:28.121
And it was the turning point between the old Juan,

27
00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.881
just a programmer, and the Juan of now,

28
00:01:31.881 --> 00:01:33.520
almost a founder.

29
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.065
I'm truly grateful for this experience:

30
00:01:38.065 --> 00:01:42.377
I learned a lot from a lot of people,

31
00:01:42.377 --> 00:01:45.058
and a lot about myself.
